## Determine IP Address

From the running target, execute `ifconfig`.


### Virtual Target

The IP address of a virtual target appears in the `vtnet0` section after `inet`; in this example, it is `192.168.122.146`.

Example Output on Virtual Target:

```bash
enc0: flags=0<> metric 0 mtu 1536
        groups: enc
        nd6 options=21<PERFORMNUD,AUTO_LINKLOCAL>
lo0: flags=8049<UP,LOOPBACK,RUNNING,MULTICAST> metric 0 mtu 16384
        options=680003<RXCSUM,TXCSUM,LINKSTATE,RXCSUM_IPV6,TXCSUM_IPV6>
        inet 127.0.0.1 netmask 0xff000000
        inet6 ::1 prefixlen 128
        inet6 fe80::1%lo0 prefixlen 64 scopeid 0x2
        groups: lo
        nd6 options=21<PERFORMNUD,AUTO_LINKLOCAL>
pflog0: flags=0<> metric 0 mtu 33144
        groups: pflog
pfsync0: flags=0<> metric 0 mtu 1500
        syncpeer: 0.0.0.0 maxupd: 128 defer: off
        syncok: 1
        groups: pfsync
vtnet0: flags=8863<UP,BROADCAST,RUNNING,SIMPLEX,MULTICAST> metric 0 mtu 1500
        options=4c07bb<RXCSUM,TXCSUM,VLAN_MTU,VLAN_HWTAGGING,JUMBO_MTU,VLAN_HWCSUM,TSO4,TSO6,LRO,VLAN_HWTSO,LINKSTATE,TXCSUM_IPV6>
        ether 52:54:00:75:e8:8f
        inet6 fe80::5054:ff:fe75:e88f%vtnet0 prefixlen 64 scopeid 0x5
        inet 192.168.122.146 netmask 0xffffff00 broadcast 192.168.122.255
        media: Ethernet autoselect (10Gbase-T <full-duplex>)
        status: active
        nd6 options=1<PERFORMNUD>
```

### Physical Target

## Visual Studio Code: Connect to target via SSH



### Prereqs

- Raspberry Pi 4
  - Ethernet connection
  - Serial connection

Get image from software center

### Confirm Target is Running

- Connect over serial - from RazPi to computer over USB

From command line:

```bash
# Confirm target is connected
(linux): ls /dev/ttyUSB*
/dev/tty/ttyUSB0

#
(linux): sudo screen /dev/ttyUSB0 115200
[sudo] password for username:

# uname -a
QNX localhost 8.0.0 YYYY/MM/DD-hh:mm:ssEST RaspberryPi4B aarch64le
```


